title: Status
new-page: true
is-special: true
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.unemployed) {
    Q.unemployed_2 = Q.unemployed.toFixed(1);
}
if (Q.inflation) {
    Q.inflation_2 = Q.inflation.toFixed(1);
}
Q.economic_growth_2 = '0';
if (Q.economic_growth) {
    Q.economic_growth_2 = Q.economic_growth.toFixed(1);
}
!}

= Status

[+ month : month +] [+ year +]

Organizational resources available: [+ resources +]

Coalition position: [? if not dem_president and not dem_house and not dem_senate : full opposition ?][? if dem_president or dem_house or dem_senate : holding [? if dem_president : the presidency ?][? if dem_president and (dem_house or dem_senate) : , ?][? if dem_house : the House ?][? if dem_house and dem_senate : , ?][? if dem_senate : the Senate ?] ?]

Insurgent influence within the coalition: [? if primary_winner_faction == "insurgent" : the last nominee came from our wing ?][? if primary_winner_faction != "insurgent" : the party establishment still controls the nomination ?]

Internal coalition dissent: [+ dissent_percent : dissent +]

= Government

President: [+ president +] ([+ president_party +])

[? if dem_president : The White House is held by our coalition. ?][? if not dem_president : The White House is held by the opposition. ?]

Congress:

House: Democrats [+ dem_house_seats +] - Republicans [+ gop_house_seats +] ([? if dem_house : Democratic majority ?][? if not dem_house : Republican majority?])

Senate: Democrats [+ dem_senate_seats +] - Republicans [+ gop_senate_seats +] ([? if dem_senate : Democratic majority ?][? if not dem_senate : Republican majority?])

{!<span class="tooltip-text" title="The Supreme Court is not up for direct election, and acts as an independent check on the elected branches, the way the Weimar presidency could act independently of the Reichstag.">Supreme Court composition</span>!}: [+ scotus_composition : scotus +]

[? if scotus_hostile : The Court has shown itself willing to strike down or block our legislative wins. ?]

Next election: [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +] ([+ next_election_type +])

= Economics

Inflation: [+ inflation_2 +]%

Unemployment: [+ unemployed_2 +]%

Economic growth: [+ economic_growth_2 +]%

Median household income: $[+ income +]

@politics

= Inter-party Relations

{!<span class="tooltip-text" title="The traditional, business-oriented wing of the Republican Party, as distinct from its Trumpist wing.">Republican establishment</span>!}: [+ gop_estab_relation : relationships +]

{!<span class="tooltip-text" title="A small party that competes with us for left-wing votes, mostly as a spoiler risk rather than a mass alternative.">Green Party</span>!}: [+ green_relation : relationships +]

{!<span class="tooltip-text" title="A minor right-leaning party that draws mostly from disaffected Republicans.">Libertarian Party</span>!}: [+ libertarian_relation : relationships +]

= The Republican Party

{!<span class="tooltip-text" title="The share of the Republican coalition currently aligned with Trumpism, as opposed to the traditional/establishment wing. This can be moved by improving relations with the establishment wing, or by Trumpist electoral defeats.">Trumpist (MAGA) share of the GOP</span>!}: [+ maga_share +]%

Establishment share of the GOP: [+ gop_estab_share +]%

{!<span class="tooltip-text" title="Trump's personal grip on the party, distinct from the size of the Trumpist wing as a whole.">Trump's personal dominance</span>!}: [+ trump_dominance +]%

= Internal Factions of the Coalition

{!<span class="tooltip-text" title="Democratic-socialist insurgents (DSA/Squad-aligned). Our home faction. Favors primarying unfriendly incumbents and building durable movement infrastructure alongside electoral work.">Insurgent</span>!} strength: [+ insurgent_strength : strength +], dissent: [+ insurgent_dissent : dissent +] [? if insurgent_split : (has split off as [+ insurgent_split_name +]) ?]

{!<span class="tooltip-text" title="Structural reformers in the Warren lane. Wants big legislative change through conventional means, wary of primarying friendly incumbents.">Progressive</span>!} strength: [+ progressive_strength : strength +], dissent: [+ progressive_dissent : dissent +] [? if progressive_split : (has split off as [+ progressive_split_name +]) ?]

{!<span class="tooltip-text" title="Union-rooted, materially focused. Sometimes to the right of insurgents culturally, but firmly to the left economically.">Labor Left</span>!} strength: [+ labor_left_strength : strength +], dissent: [+ labor_left_dissent : dissent +] [? if labor_left_split : (has split off as [+ labor_left_split_name +]) ?]

{!<span class="tooltip-text" title="Coalition managers in the Obama/Biden lane. Cannot split off from the party - they define what 'the party as it is' means.">Establishment Democrat</span>!} strength: [+ establishment_dem_strength : strength +], dissent: [+ establishment_dem_dissent : dissent +]

{!<span class="tooltip-text" title="The right flank of the caucus, holding frontline swing districts. Constantly tempted to defect on votes that endanger their seats.">Blue Dog</span>!} strength: [+ blue_dog_strength : strength +], dissent: [+ blue_dog_dissent : dissent +] [? if blue_dog_split : (has split off as [+ blue_dog_split_name +]) ?]


@movement
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.canvass_strength) {
    Q.canvass_strength_2 = Q.canvass_strength.toFixed(1);
}
if (Q.online_right_strength) {
    Q.online_right_strength_2 = Q.online_right_strength.toFixed(1);
}
!}

= Movement Infrastructure

Not literal private armies, unlike the paramilitaries of Weimar Germany - this models organizing capacity and its dark mirror on the right. Militancy here means willingness to strike or disrupt (on the left) or willingness to escalate beyond normal politics (on the right), not routine street violence.

{!<span class="tooltip-text" title="DSA and allied labor organizing, canvassing, and mutual aid capacity.">Canvass Network</span>!} Strength: [+ canvass_strength_2 +] thousand active volunteers

Canvass Network Militancy: [+ canvass_militancy : militancy +]

{!<span class="tooltip-text" title="Online-to-street right-wing mobilization infrastructure.">Online Right</span>!} Strength: [+ online_right_strength_2 +] thousand active participants

Online Right Militancy: [+ online_right_militancy : militancy +]

Union density: [+ union_density +]% of the workforce

= Federal Institutions

{!<span class="tooltip-text" title="Loyalty to the constitutional order and democratic norms, not to any one party.">Federal agencies loyalty</span>!}: [+ federal_agencies_loyalty : loyalty +]

National Guard loyalty: [+ national_guard_loyalty : loyalty +]

@polls
# Always recompute vote share before displaying, rather than trusting that
# some other scene already ran election_algorithm recently - this avoids a
# real bug found in testing where the polls tab could show a stale or
# all-zero result if nothing else had triggered the algorithm yet this game.
set-jump: status.polls_display
go-to: election_algorithm

@polls_display
on-arrival: {!
Q.pro_democracy_disp = Math.round(Q.pro_democracy);
Q.polarization_disp = Math.round(Q.polarization);
Q.socialism_disp = Math.round(Q.socialism);
!}

= Projected election results

(if the general election were held now):

Democratic: [+ dem_votes +]%

Republican: [+ gop_votes +]%

Green: [+ green_votes +]%

Libertarian: [+ libertarian_votes +]%

Others: [+ other_votes +]%

**Detailed results for each demographic**

Working class: Dem: [+ working_class_dem_display +]%, GOP: [+ working_class_gop_display +]%, Green: [+ working_class_green_display +]%, Libertarian: [+ working_class_libertarian_display +]%, Others: [+ working_class_other_display +]%

College educated: Dem: [+ college_educated_dem_display +]%, GOP: [+ college_educated_gop_display +]%, Green: [+ college_educated_green_display +]%, Libertarian: [+ college_educated_libertarian_display +]%, Others: [+ college_educated_other_display +]%

Non-college white: Dem: [+ non_college_white_dem_display +]%, GOP: [+ non_college_white_gop_display +]%, Green: [+ non_college_white_green_display +]%, Libertarian: [+ non_college_white_libertarian_display +]%, Others: [+ non_college_white_other_display +]%

Black voters: Dem: [+ black_voters_dem_display +]%, GOP: [+ black_voters_gop_display +]%, Green: [+ black_voters_green_display +]%, Libertarian: [+ black_voters_libertarian_display +]%, Others: [+ black_voters_other_display +]%

Latino voters: Dem: [+ latino_voters_dem_display +]%, GOP: [+ latino_voters_gop_display +]%, Green: [+ latino_voters_green_display +]%, Libertarian: [+ latino_voters_libertarian_display +]%, Others: [+ latino_voters_other_display +]%

Suburban: Dem: [+ suburban_dem_display +]%, GOP: [+ suburban_gop_display +]%, Green: [+ suburban_green_display +]%, Libertarian: [+ suburban_libertarian_display +]%, Others: [+ suburban_other_display +]%

Rural: Dem: [+ rural_dem_display +]%, GOP: [+ rural_gop_display +]%, Green: [+ rural_green_display +]%, Libertarian: [+ rural_libertarian_display +]%, Others: [+ rural_other_display +]%

Support for democratic norms: [+ pro_democracy_disp +]%

Polarization: [+ polarization_disp +]%

Public sympathy for economic-left ideas: [+ socialism_disp +]%

@primary_polls
# Same fix as @polls above - always recompute before displaying.
set-jump: status.primary_polls_display
go-to: election_algorithm.primary_algorithm

@primary_polls_display

